  "slug": "concurrence-graph-spectra-d812",
  "summary": "Five preprints from 23–24 November 2026 pair simulation platforms with spectroscopic or numerical probes of interacting many-body phases and dynamics.",
  "synthesis": "The items share a focus on characterizing interacting quantum many-body systems through simulation and structured probes. Cold-atom work reports coherent meson-baryon conversion in a 1D SU(2) quantum link model and proposes site-resolved, lattice-modulation signatures of a rung-Mott insulator in bosonic two-leg ladders. A hybrid qubit-boson Trotterized circuit simulates Jaynes-Cummings-Hubbard dynamics, benchmarked against exact diagonalization. Quantum Monte Carlo for 2D dipolar excitons yields an analytical framework for chemical potential and interaction energies. Liouvillian quasiparticle spectroscopy extends spectral concepts to open systems, with protocols and numerical validation. The novelty lies in pairing each system with a measurable observable or benchmark rather than in a single shared method; the connection to concurrence or graph spectra is not evident from these summaries.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-26"
}
